  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Added dimension-generic, nonempty top-left fmpz matrix prefix adapters for caller-owned HNF, SNF, HNF transforms, and exact row-LLL transforms. Every adapter validates alias and capacity constraints before mutation, scopes and clears FLINT windows, refreshes retained-byte accounting on writable roots, and is exposed through generated dynamic and source-transparent native bindings. Focused tests cover changing-prefix reuse, exact transform identities, rejection atomicity, big-integer accounting, one shared native arena, and 300 sanitizer lifecycle cycles.",
    "risks": [
      "The new operations are currently host-native only; Wasm remains an explicitly classified exact ordinary fallback pending a separate authenticated production-closure receipt.",
      "The exhaustive changed-file run passed build, architecture, unit, compiler, direct FLINT, sanitizer, and native lifecycle checks before failing unrelated dense-rational performance budgets for select_rows, select_columns, and stack under concurrent system load. The focused adapter suite passed again against the freshly rebuilt addon."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Integrate the prefix calls into the cubic relation/unit scheduler by preallocating roots to its chosen maximum capacity, including factor-count plus 18, and passing the current logical row and column counts.",
      "Enable Wasm only after these exact prefix operations enter an authenticated production closure with platform evidence."
    ]
  }
